targets-page-title = Targets
targets-intro = Swedish targets first, then the US set. A badge means a measurement is still missing or not confirmed. The picture uses the length unit in the header. Print goes through a PDF at a stated scale, with a bar you can measure.
open-items = Still to measure
open-items-intro = These stay visible until the measurement is in the app. Editing a shape does not clear the badge.
badge-placeholder = Placeholder
badge-unverified = Unverified
badge-resolved = Official
flag-T2 = Moose hit-area outline is a rough stand-in, about 60 by 47 cm, not a measurement and not for scoring.
flag-T3 = Moose silhouette size, placement, and siamese spacing are not measured. The shape is decorative and not for scoring.
flag-T4 = Roe-buck rings 10, 15 and 20 cm are the published SJF figures and still need confirming on an owned target. The oval is a stand-in, not the figure.
flag-T5-outline = The outline is not measured. Rings are drawn only where a diameter is published.
flag-T5-all = No official dimensions are in Holdover for this target. Nothing is invented.
flag-T5-viltmal = SvSF or ISSF ring diameters are not in Holdover. They are not invented.
flag-T5-300 = The international 300 m ring diameters are not in Holdover. They are not invented.
flag-T5-field = The rectangle is the published width and height. The figure inside an official target is not measured.
flag-T6 = No official red-deer or fallow-deer figure was found. Choose a vital-zone diameter yourself. There is no default.
flag-US-IPSC = IPSC/USPSA dimensions are not confirmed against the current rulebook, so none are drawn.
flag-US-IDPA = IDPA dimensions are not confirmed against the current rulebook, so none are drawn.
flag-US-STEEL = IPSC steel dimensions are not confirmed against the current rulebook, so none are drawn.
flag-US-RECT = A rectangular plate has no fixed size here. Set one when you know the plate you shoot.
flag-user-edit = Your edit. This is still not a measured official target.
target-no-size = No published size yet
target-edit-title = Edit placeholder
target-edit-intro = Points are centimetres from the ring centre, in the length unit selected above. Saving stores your copy and keeps the badge.
target-points = Points
target-points-tip = One point per line, horizontal then vertical, in the current length unit. The origin is the ring centre.
target-no-points = This target has no outline to edit yet. Add a vital-zone diameter where that applies, or import a drawing.
target-label-tip = Name for your copy.
