about-intro = Holdover is a personal ballistic calculator and equipment notebook. Predictions come from the model and your inputs. Confirm them with live fire.
about-version = Version
about-mit-heading = Holdover licence
about-mit = Holdover is MIT. Copyright (c) 2026 Patrik Hallgren. The text below is the same as the LICENSE file.
about-personal = Holdover is personal and non-commercial. It has no account and no telemetry. The only network call is the weather fetch you start.
about-weather-heading = Weather data
about-drag-heading = Drag tables
about-drag = The G1, G2, G5, G6, G7 and G8 Cd–Mach tables are from the JBM Ballistics downloads page (https://www.jbmballistics.com/downloads.html). JBM states that the files on that page are free for public use. JBM obtained them from the US Army Ballistic Research Laboratory via Robert L. McCoy. They are the only bundled ballistic data. GL is not included.
about-crates-heading = Third-party software
about-crates = Direct crates linked by this build: tauri 2 (Apache-2.0 OR MIT), rusqlite 0.32.1 (MIT), serde and serde_json (MIT OR Apache-2.0), ureq 2.12.1 (MIT OR Apache-2.0), uuid 1.11.0 (Apache-2.0 OR MIT), sha2 0.10.9 (MIT OR Apache-2.0), clap 4.5 (MIT OR Apache-2.0), zip 2.6.1 (MIT), image 0.25.10 (MIT OR Apache-2.0), kamadak-exif 0.6.1 (BSD-2-Clause). Other crates come in through those and keep the licences recorded in Cargo.lock. The window has no npm packages. WebKitGTK and GTK come from the system packages and are not copied into Holdover. py-ballisticcalc 3.1.1 (LGPL-3.0) is a CI test oracle and is not installed with the app.
about-limits-heading = Known limitations
about-limits = These items are still open. T2: the moose hit-area outline is a placeholder. T3: the moose silhouette size and where the rings sit on it are unmeasured. T4: roe-buck rings 10, 15 and 20 cm are the published figures and are not confirmed on an owned target; the oval is a stand-in. T5: other owned official targets are unmeasured. T6: red deer and fallow deer have no official diameter, so none is invented. US rulebook targets (IPSC/USPSA, IDPA, and steel) have no confirmed size; that waits on ruler photos. Aerodynamic jump can be requested and is not applied.
about-keys = Keyboard: Ctrl+K opens the screen list, Ctrl+U cycles the unit preset, and Solve keeps its letter shortcuts. A focused control shows the accent outline. The text scale follows the Omarchy text-size knob, and Larger text adds a step on top.
about-package = The application menu starts /usr/bin/holdover. A shell still runs ~/.local/bin/holdover when that directory is earlier on PATH. Both use the same library at ~/.local/share/holdover/holdover.db.
settings-about = About, licences, and known limitations.
